    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "A woman is three times as old as her daughter. In four years’ time she will be only two and a half times as old as her daughter. What is the woman’s present age?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "36 years",
      "worked": "Let $x$ years be the daughter’s present age. The woman’s present age is $3x$ years. In four years, their ages will be $x+4$ and $3x+4$ years.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3x+4&=\\frac{5}{2}(x+4)\\\\6x+8&=5x+20\\\\6x-5x&=20-8\\\\x&=12\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe woman’s present age is $3\\times12=36$ years.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
